    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nWhen `cmdheight=0` and surround is configured with `respect_selection_type = true`, linewise surround results in a hit enter prompt.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-1028+gd422fc8274\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `:set cmdheight=0`\r\n2. Configure surround with `respect_selection_type = true`\r\n3. Linewise select 3 or more lines\r\n4. Add surrounding \n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo hit enter prompt when linewise surrounding 3 or more lines.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nHit enter prompt showing the result of indent when surrounding. Ex: `3 lines >ed 1 time`.\r\n\r\nIf the output of the shift command is not needed then I think the command could be prepended with `silent`",
